      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143497",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{15}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n$f(x; \u03b8) = \u03b8x^{- \u03b8 - 1}, x \\ge 1$,\nwhere $\u03b8$ is an unknown parameter. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{15}$, you're given that\n$\u220f_(i = 1)^(15)x_{i} = 40.6$.\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
